# particlelab.numos — ParticleLab (app id 15) captures for paadweb/public/apps/index.html
#
# The website lists 3 shots for this app (source of truth: DELIVERABLES.md):
#   1. /assets/img/apps/particle-1.webp — molten pool + water: steam, stone, heat glow
#   2. /assets/img/apps/particle-2.webp — heater/cooler/C4 wired in the sand
#   3. /assets/img/apps/particle-3.webp — plant climbing to water, palette overlay open
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BLOCKER: ParticleLab is a DEAD CARD in the emulator build this script runs on.
# It cannot be launched, so no app frame can be asserted or captured. Evidence:
#   * platformio.ini [env:emulator_pc] build_src_filter is a per-file whitelist
#     (platformio.ini:412-560). It lists Calculation, Calculus, Equations,
#     Settings, Statistics, Probability, Sequences, Regression, Grapher,
#     GameBoy, Notes, AiApp ... but NOT apps/ParticleLabApp.cpp nor
#     apps/ParticleEngine.cpp -> the app is not compiled into the binary.
#     Confirmed against the build tree: C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/src/apps/
#     contains no ParticleLabApp.o and no ParticleEngine.o, and strings on
#     NativeHal.o contain zero "particle" hits.
#   * The emulator's own router src/hal/NativeHal.cpp:1338 launchApp() has no
#     case 15 -> default prints "[APP] App 15 no implementada en simulador"
#     (observed live by the probe run) and g_mode stays MENU. NativeHal has no
#     AppMode for it at all (grep PARTICLE in NativeHal.cpp = 0 hits).
#   * The script grammar cannot reach it either: open_app/assert_app resolve
#     names through scriptAppNameToId()/canonicalAppName() (NativeHal.cpp:2192,
#     2229) and neither has a particlelab entry -> `open_app particlelab` is a
#     parse error (exit 2), so it cannot even be attempted.
#   * The emulator's context model has no slot for it either: numos::Ctx /
#     ctxName() / ctxSlug() in src/ui/AppContext.h:42-123 list 17 contexts and
#     ParticleLab is not one of them, so no assert_app name could ever match an
#     active ParticleLab frame.
#   * Documented the same way in docs/specs/NUMOS_EMULATOR_APP_ENABLEMENT_
#     PARITY_SPEC.md:128 ("ParticleLab (15) ... dead card ... defer") and
#     NUMOS_EMULATOR_PER_APP_ENABLEMENT_MATRIX.md:498 (enablement "none").
#
# What this script DOES prove: the launcher reaches the ParticleLab card
# (assert_menu_focus resolves against the real APPS[] table, id 15), the launch
# is attempted with ENTER, and the launch is rejected (the same focus assert
# still passes afterwards => we are still in Menu, mode never changed).
#
# No website shot is written. A frame of the launcher, the calculator or any
# other screen is NOT particle-1/2/3.webp; a plausible-looking capture of the
# wrong screen would ship to the site. The single PPM written below is a
# DIAGNOSTIC of the launcher with the ParticleLab card focused. It is slug-
# prefixed (particlelab-...) so it cannot collide with a parallel run, and it
# deliberately does NOT use the `shots-particlelab-<n>.ppm` name the website
# deliverables use, so nothing can pick it up as particle-1/2/3.webp.
#
# Theme: ParticleLab has no casio-specific code (docs/theme-manager-casio.md:106
# "custom-draw engine / OFF") — it would render numos only, so assert_theme
# numos is asserted before the diagnostic capture.
#
# Run (repo root):
#   ./"C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/program" --headless --deterministic \
#       --script tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/particlelab.numos \
#       --fs-root tests/emulator/fs --frames 1400 --quiet
#
# Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 script/parse error · 3 screenshot write error · 4 assertion failure.

log "particlelab: waiting for launcher"
wait 200
assert_app Menu

# ParticleLab is index 15 of APPS[] and the numos launcher is a 3-column grid:
#   row 0: Calculation, Grapher, Equations
#   row 1: Calculus, Statistics, Probability
#   row 2: Regression, Sequences, Python
#   row 3: Matrices, Settings, Chemistry
#   row 4: Bridge, Circuit, Fluid 2D
#   row 5: ParticleLab, Neural Lab, OpticsLab
# From Calculation (row 0, col 0): DOWN x5 lands on ParticleLab (row 5, col 0).
key down
wait 5
key down
wait 5
key down
wait 5
key down
wait 5
key down
wait 5

# Proves the navigation by resolving the card name against the real APPS[]
# table: focus is on id 15 "ParticleLab".
assert_menu_focus ParticleLab
assert_theme numos

# Attempt the launch exactly the way the firmware does (ENTER -> CLICKED ->
# launchApp(15)).
key enter
wait 60

# If the app had launched, g_mode would have left MENU and this assert would
# FAIL with "assert_menu_focus requiere el launcher (Menu) activo". It passes
# => the launcher rejected the card: NativeHal printed "[APP] App 15 no
# implementada en simulador". This is the blocker, asserted.
assert_app Menu
assert_menu_focus ParticleLab
assert_theme numos

# DIAGNOSTIC ONLY — launcher with the ParticleLab card focused (id 15). Not a
# website shot: none of particle-1/2/3.webp is produced by this script, and
# this path does not match the shots-particlelab-<n>.ppm deliverable names.
screenshot out/particlelab-diag-blocked-launcher.ppm
log "particlelab: launch attempt rejected by emulator (App 15 no implementada) - no website shot possible"
log "particlelab: done"
